------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Algorithms ported into eve's portable code (provenance as each file states)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. src/eve/net/ed25519.cljc — Ed25519 after TweetNaCl's construction
   (https://tweetnacl.cr.yp.to/, released into the public domain by its
   authors).

3. src/eve/net/xxh3.cljc — XXH3-128, ported from the ValueScript kernel's
   xxhash.vs (atom.broker). The algorithm is xxHash's
   (https://github.com/Cyan4973/xxHash, Yann Collet).

4. src/eve/net/poseidon2.cljc, src/eve/net/bn254.cljc — Poseidon2 over BN254;
   the round constants were copied mechanically from the Noir poseidon2
   package vendored in atom.broker (aegis/noir/vendor/poseidon2), whose
   upstream is https://github.com/TaceoLabs/noir-poseidon (constants from
   https://github.com/HorizenLabs/poseidon2). No license file was vendored
   with that package; the release manager confirms its upstream license
   before eve is published.

5. src/eve/net/sha256.cljc, src/eve/net/sha512.cljc, src/eve/net/aes.cljc —
   written from FIPS 180-4 and FIPS 197.

